# Cursor activity sources (QuotAI)

## Runtime / product

QuotAI uses the **local Cursor Agent Host log** (and meter snapshots / pace history) only.

- No CSV import
- No shipping dependency on usage exports
- Do not design features that require the user to keep dropping CSVs

## Usage CSV in chat / research

Any usage export looked at in chat is a **research aid only**: reverse-engineer whether a billing/label signal already exists (or can be derived) in the local log. If it does, teach the parser; if it does not, leave the gap explicit.

Field notes: `.scratch/quotai/research/usage-csv-fields.md`

## Model display / store

Source of the string shown in the discrepancy strip is the **local Agent Host `modelId`**, with one rewrite: `default` → `auto`.

| Local log has | Show / store |
| --- | --- |
| `default` | `auto` |
| Full id (e.g. `claude-sonnet-5-5-medium`) | That full id |
| Short / base id (e.g. `glm-5p3-flash`) | That short id — do **not** invent `-high` / `-low` / `-thinking-*` |

Never upgrade a short local id via CSV timestamp join (or any heuristic) when the variant is ambiguous. Do not reclassify third-party `modelId`s onto Cursor Models because a Task ran “under Auto.”
